{%- comment -%}
  Zaria - robots.txt.

  While Theme settings > Search engines > "Let search engines index the site" is off, the whole
  site is refused to every crawler. The shop is not open and a half-built catalogue indexed now
  would have to be unpicked later. Tick that switch at launch and this file falls back to
  Shopify's own rules, sitemap line and all, with nothing else to change.

  The meta robots tag in layout/theme.liquid reads the same switch. Both are needed: this file
  stops the crawl, the tag covers anything that arrives by a link rather than by the crawl.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if settings.seo_allow_indexing -%}
{% for group in robots.default_groups %}
{{- group.user_agent }}
{% for rule in group.rules %}{{ rule }}
{% endfor %}{%- if group.sitemap != blank %}{{ group.sitemap }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{%- else -%}
# The shop is not open yet. Please do not index it.
User-agent: *
Disallow: /
{%- endif -%}
